			</h2>

			<p class="text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-body">
				Knowing that you read at <strong class="font-semibold text-ink">238 WPM</strong> is useful, but most people plan their study sessions and book goals in <strong class="font-semibold text-ink">pages</strong>, not words. Because page density changes depending on font size, margins, and book format, converting WPM into pages per hour requires a clear baseline.
			</p>

			<p class="text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-body">
				In publishing and academic writing, two standard benchmarks apply:
			</p>

			<ul class="list-disc space-y-2.5 pl-6 text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-body">
				<li>
					<strong class="font-semibold text-ink">Standard Double-Spaced Page (Essays, Reports, Manuscripts):</strong> Averages <strong class="font-semibold text-ink">250 words per page</strong>.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong class="font-semibold text-ink">Standard Trade Paperback / Non-Fiction Book Page:</strong> Averages <strong class="font-semibold text-ink">275 to 300 words per page</strong> (we use <strong class="font-semibold text-ink">300 words per page</strong> below for realistic book planning).
				</li>
			</ul>

			<p class="text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-body">
				At the adult average of <strong class="font-semibold text-ink">238 WPM</strong>, you read <strong class="font-semibold text-ink">14,280 words per hour</strong>, which works out to roughly <strong class="font-semibold text-ink">47.6 paperback pages per hour</strong> (just under 0.8 pages per minute).
			</p>

